I wrote:
| So what is the trick?  Why is it important to hold him on another level
| temporarily?  He will just teleport directly to you when he gets
| free/resurrected anyway.  (Don't forget spoiler warnings.)

In article <8177@star.cs.vu.nl>, lbkruij@cs.vu.nl,
Lucas Kruijswijk replied:
| Do not go back to that level! Levels other than your current level are saved
| in nethack and will not be updated. If you return, there is 1 big update,
| corpses rot and monsters get hitpoints. Some monsters can follow you if you
| change from level (shopkeepers, the Wizard, ghosts etc.), but only in that
| particular moment that you change from level. If the Wizard is on an other
| level than your level he can't go to you and he can't reincarnate (because
| he is still alive).

One giant AHA!  (And throw in a "Now why didn't I figgur' that?".)

